% I. INTRODUCTION / NATURE OF ACTION
% ===================================================================
\section{NATURE OF ACTION}

\para Plaintiff Ashle' Antoinette Penn brings this employment discrimination action against Defendant Central City Concern for violations of Oregon Revised Statutes Chapter 659A, including unlawful retaliation, interference with protected leave rights, failure to accommodate disability, and constructive discharge following Plaintiff's exercise of protected rights under Oregon employment laws.

\para This Court has jurisdiction over this matter pursuant to ORS 659A.885, which grants exclusive original jurisdiction to Oregon circuit courts for civil actions alleging violations of ORS 659A.001 to 659A.665.

% ===================================================================
% II. PARTIES
% ===================================================================
\section{PARTIES}

\para Plaintiff Ashle' Antoinette Penn (hereinafter ``Plaintiff'' or ``Ms. Penn'') is an individual residing in Multnomah County, Oregon.

\para Defendant Central City Concern (hereinafter ``Defendant'' or ``CCC'') is an Oregon nonprofit corporation with its principal place of business located at 232 NW Sixth Avenue, Portland, Oregon 97209.

\para At all times relevant to this Complaint, Defendant was Plaintiff's employer within the meaning of ORS 659A.001(6) and employed more than six employees, thereby subjecting it to the prohibitions against discrimination and retaliation under ORS Chapter 659A.

% ===================================================================
% III. JURISDICTION AND VENUE
% ===================================================================
\section{JURISDICTION AND VENUE}

\para This Court has subject matter jurisdiction over Plaintiff's claims pursuant to ORS 659A.885, which vests exclusive original jurisdiction in Oregon circuit courts for civil actions alleging violations of ORS 659A.001 to 659A.665.

\para Venue is proper in Multnomah County pursuant to ORS 14.080 because Defendant's principal place of business is located in Multnomah County and the acts and omissions giving rise to Plaintiff's claims occurred in Multnomah County.

\para Plaintiff timely filed a complaint with the Oregon Bureau of Labor and Industries (``BOLI'') on or about May 5, 2025.

\para On or about August 18, 2025, BOLI issued Plaintiff a Final Order Dismissing Complaint without a hearing and a Notice of Right to File a Civil Action.

\para This Complaint is filed within 90 days of Plaintiff's receipt of the BOLI Notice of Right to File a Civil Action, satisfying the jurisdictional prerequisites of ORS 659A.820.

