\section*{SECOND CLAIM FOR RELIEF}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{SECOND CLAIM FOR RELIEF}
\centerline{\textbf{Unlawful Interference with Protected Leave Rights}}
\centerline{\textbf{(ORS 659A.186)}}

\para Plaintiff realleges and incorporates by reference each and every allegation contained in paragraphs 1 through [XX] as though fully set forth herein.

\para ORS 659A.186 prohibits employers from interfering with, restraining, or denying the exercise of or the attempt to exercise any right protected under ORS 659A.150 to 659A.186.

\para Plaintiff exercised her protected right to take family leave under ORS 659A.156.

\para Defendant interfered with Plaintiff's exercise of protected leave rights by:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1in, itemsep=0pt]
\item Creating a false performance record based on alleged failures that occurred during approved protected leave when Plaintiff had no duty to work;
\item Delaying Plaintiff's reinstatement to her position for 38 days following the conclusion of protected leave;
\item Conditioning Plaintiff's return to work on completion of accommodation paperwork despite no such requirement existing prior to her leave;
\item Threatening Plaintiff with termination for taking protected leave; and
\item Creating a hostile work environment upon Plaintiff's return designed to punish her for exercising leave rights.
\end{itemize}

\para Defendant's fabrication of performance issues during Plaintiff's approved leave period, followed by use of those fabricated issues to justify adverse actions, constituted interference with Plaintiff's exercise of protected leave rights because it deterred Plaintiff and would deter other employees from taking protected leave in the future.

\para As a direct and proximate result of Defendant's unlawful interference with protected leave rights, Plaintiff has suffered and continues to suffer economic damages including lost wages, lost benefits, and diminished earning capacity, the full amount of which will be proven at trial but is believed to exceed \$500,000.

\para As a direct and proximate result of Defendant's unlawful interference, Plaintiff has suffered and continues to suffer noneconomic damages including emotional distress, humiliation, loss of reputation, and other compensable harm, the full amount of which will be proven at trial.

