\section*{FIFTH CLAIM FOR RELIEF}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{FIFTH CLAIM FOR RELIEF}
\centerline{\textbf{Constructive Discharge}}
\centerline{\textbf{(ORS 659A.030, ORS 659A.082, ORS 659A.112)}}

\para Plaintiff realleges and incorporates by reference each and every allegation contained in paragraphs 1 through [XX] as though fully set forth herein.

\para Defendant intentionally created working conditions so intolerable and discriminatory that a reasonable person in Plaintiff's position would have felt compelled to resign.

\para Defendant's creation of intolerable conditions included:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1in, itemsep=0pt]
\item Fabricating performance deficiencies that allegedly occurred while Plaintiff was on protected leave;
\item Orchestrating a workplace boycott by instructing managers not to work with Plaintiff;
\item Making it impossible for Plaintiff to perform her essential job functions by denying her access to necessary colleagues;
\item Subjecting Plaintiff to a 38-day delay in reinstatement following protected leave;
\item Conditioning Plaintiff's accommodation and return to work on acceptance of false performance improvement demands; and
\item Creating a hostile work environment designed to force Plaintiff's resignation.
\end{itemize}

\para A reasonable person in Plaintiff's position, facing fabricated performance allegations, systematic workplace exclusion, and denial of necessary working conditions, would have found continued employment intolerable.

\para As a direct and proximate result of being constructively discharged, Plaintiff has suffered and continues to suffer economic damages including lost wages, lost benefits, and diminished earning capacity, the full amount of which will be proven at trial but is believed to exceed \$500,000.

\para As a direct and proximate result of being constructively discharged, Plaintiff has suffered and continues to suffer noneconomic damages including emotional distress, humiliation, loss of reputation, and other compensable harm, the full amount of which will be proven at trial.

